carry `patent_flag = 1`.

WHAT WE TOOK FROM UNIPROT, AND WHAT WE CHANGED
CC BY 4.0 requires that changes be indicated. Per field, from `provenance.tsv`:

  * `name` and `aliases` on the natural-protein rows are UniProt's -- the gene
    symbol where the entry has one, the recommended or submission name
    otherwise, with every other name UniProt offers kept as an alias.
  * `reference_aa` on those rows is UniProt's canonical sequence string.
  * `peptide_anchor` on the curated designed-part rows records that the residue
    offset of a peptide inside its parent protein was read out of a UniProt
    canonical. No UniProt string is stored in those rows; the position is.

  Changes made: we selected single entries from a much larger database; we
  discarded every cross-reference that was not an EMBL ProteinId, so that no
  KEGG, DrugBank, ChEMBL or DrugCentral identifier is carried into this dataset
  under UniProt's licence; we paired each protein with an independently fetched
  nucleotide CDS and kept only cross-references whose CDS translates to the
  canonical exactly; and we wrote every description ourselves. Descriptions,
  boundary rules and record ids are not UniProt's and are marked `own-work`.

